{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}]},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"heading","anchor":"Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"View","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"text":" to that file.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Instantiate and register","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add state, action case, and register","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"text":"The Decision Rule","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2},{"style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}]}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Arc